The code statements that lead to the bug are:
mt7915_coredump_unregister(dev);
// followed by in another path: vfree(dev->coredump.crash_data)
// and in work item: crash_data-> // UAF
Reason:
The race occurs because `mt7915_coredump_unregister()` frees `dev->coredump.crash_data` without first ensuring that the work item `mt7915_mac_dump_work()` has finished executing. The work item later dereferences the freed `crash_data`, causing a use-after-free.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
cancel_work_sync(&dev->dump_work);
mt7915_coredump_unregister(dev);
Reason:
Adding `cancel_work_sync(&dev->dump_work)` before `mt7915_coredump_unregister()` ensures that any pending or executing dump work is completed or cancelled before the crash data is freed, eliminating the race condition.

